    untreatedTrajectory: "Hartnett, Nelson & Rinn (2004) demonstrated experimentally that graduate counseling students shown a case with overlapping gifted/ADHD features tended to converge on an ADHD diagnosis, evidence that diagnostic confusion between giftedness and ADHD is real. Rinn & Reynolds (2012) then provided empirical data linking Dabrowskian overexcitabilities to ADHD-like symptom scores in gifted adolescents, showing why the two can be conflated in either direction, missing a true ADHD in a gifted child or over-attributing ADHD to giftedness. Honest limitations: Hartnett et al. used a small analog vignette sample (44 participants) rather than clinical cases, and Rinn & Reynolds is a correlational self-report study, so neither establishes true misdiagnosis rates in practice.",
