    pattern: "Diagnostic reasoning identifies the disease; empathic attunement elicits the honest history, builds the trust that drives adherence, and tailors the plan to the person. In medicine the two together measurably change hard clinical outcomes, not just satisfaction scores.",
    untreatedTrajectory: "A clinically sharp but low-empathy physician gets worse biological results from equivalent patients: less disclosure, poorer adherence, and — in the data — worse metabolic control and more complications. Analytical skill alone leaves outcome on the table that empathy would have captured.",
