    connectionCase: "Structured near-peer mentorship communities improve persistence: a scalable first-year biology peer-mentorship program roughly doubled the odds of enrolling in subsequent STEM courses and improved perceived relatedness, competence, and belonging (Yomogida et al., 2021); near-peer STEM programs likewise raise belonging and science identity (Trujillo et al., 2015).",
    growthMeasures: "Peer-mentorship participants were ~2x more likely to continue in the STEM course sequence (Yomogida et al., 2021). Honest counterweight on practice itself: Macnamara et al. (2014) meta-analysis found deliberate practice explained ~26% of performance variance in games, 21% music, 18% sports, but only ~4% education and <1% professions, and just ~5% when practice was measured by logs rather than recall. So community support and structured practice help meaningfully, but neither is a sole determinant of mastery.",
