    untreatedTrajectory: "Hill & Turiano (2014, Psychological Science) used the longitudinal MIDUS sample and found that adults reporting a higher sense of purpose in life had lower mortality risk over the following 14 years, even after controlling for other facets of psychological and affective well-being — and the benefit held regardless of age or retirement status. The implication for an unsupported arc is the inverse: purpose can erode across adulthood (through role loss, retirement, isolation), and where it is not cultivated or replaced, that protective engine is simply absent.",
