    connectionCase: "The pairing case is direct: the aesthete's gift monetizes only when a Tactical/Financial partner (or developed second line) sequences and prices it. Recognizing Aesthetic as a value-driving line — not decoration — is what lets an organization staff it deliberately instead of treating it as a cost.",
    growthMeasures: "Lab: aesthetics significantly predicted perceived usability pre- and post-use (Tractinsky et al., 2000). Firm-level (business-case, not peer-reviewed): McKinsey reported top design-quartile companies with ~32% higher revenue growth and ~56% higher total shareholder returns vs. peers over five years — treat these figures as consulting analysis, not controlled evidence.",
