    connectionCase: "The clinical remedy Clance & Imes emphasized was breaking secrecy — having the person discover that similarly capable peers share the same private doubts, which disconfirms the 'I'm the only fraud here' belief. This is direct evidence that contact with recognizably same-caliber others deflates impostor feelings that isolation inflates.",
