    connectionCase: "By the same evidence, stronger social relationships are associated with reduced mortality risk, and the mechanistic reading is that connection lowers the chronic physiological load (lower inflammation, calmer cardiovascular and HPA activity) that isolation imposes (Holt-Lunstad et al. 2015; consistent with CTRA and stress-buffering mechanisms above).",
