    untreatedTrajectory: "The evidence base is still skewed West: in Naito et al. (2023), the meta-analytic pool of ~1.3 million individuals drew only ~11% of data from Asia and almost none from Africa or South America, and the authors report a RELATIVELY LOWER hazard ratio in Asian cohorts than in North American/European ones — so the effect appears attenuated, not absent, where collectivist norms and different care systems may buffer it. The direction holds cross-regionally, but the magnitude is culture- and system-dependent, and low-income regions remain largely untested.",
