    connectionCase: "Steinberg, Lamborn, Darling, Mounts & Dornbusch (1994, Child Development) tracked ~2,300 adolescents and found those with accepting, firm, democratic parents earned higher grades, were more self-reliant, and reported less anxiety, depression, and delinquency, with benefits that held across ethnicity, SES, and family structure.",
