    id: "r8-knowing-not-doing", kind: "archetype",
    name: "The Clear Diagnosis, Unexecuted",
    highLines: ["Meta-Cognitive"],
    lowLines: ["Volitional"],
    pattern: "Seeing exactly what one should do is a different faculty from making oneself do it. High self-awareness can produce a precise, honest account of the needed change that nonetheless never gets enacted, the intention-behavior gap.",
    untreatedTrajectory: "Sheeran (2002) meta-analyzed 10 meta-analyses (422 studies) and found intentions and later behavior correlate strongly (r ~ 0.53) yet still leave most of the variance in behavior unexplained, formalizing that good intentions routinely fail to convert. The meta-cognitive high without volition lives in that gap: accurate insight, chronic non-execution, and the demoralization of watching oneself not act.",
    connectionCase: "Sheeran & Webb (2016, Social and Personality Psychology Compass) locate the failure not in understanding but in translation, and catalog what actually bridges the gap, especially implementation intentions ('if situation X, then I will do Y') and other volitional strategies that pre-commit behavior to cues rather than relying on in-the-moment will. The remedy is building the volitional scaffolding, not more insight.",
    growthMeasures: "Sheeran (2002): sample-weighted intention-behavior correlation r ~ 0.53, 'large' but still leaving ~72% of behavioral variance unaccounted for. Sheeran & Webb (2016) review implementation-intention interventions with meta-analytic support for closing part of the gap. Effect sizes vary widely by behavior and population; these are averages, not guarantees.",
    sources: [
      { cite: "Sheeran, P. (2002). Intention-Behavior Relations: A Conceptual and Empirical Review. European Review of Social Psychology, 12(1), 1-36.", finding: "Meta-analysis of meta-analyses (422 studies) yields intention-behavior r ~ 0.53, quantifying a substantial gap where intentions do not translate to action. Limitation: correlational synthesis; heterogeneity across behaviors is large.", kind: "doi", ref: "https://doi.org/10.1080/14792772143000003" },
      { cite: "Sheeran, P., & Webb, T. L. (2016). The Intention-Behavior Gap. Social and Personality Psychology Compass, 10(9), 503-518.", finding: "Reviews why intentions fail and which strategies (notably implementation intentions) help close the gap. Limitation: narrative/integrative review; intervention effects vary by domain.", kind: "doi", ref: "https://doi.org/10.1111/spc3.12265" },
    ],
