    pattern: "In domains like surgery, mechanical craft, and complex sport, spatial reasoning and fine motor control jointly drive early skill: the mind that mentally rotates and orients the field guides hands that must act on structures they cannot see directly. Spatial ability gives the novice a real head start on the motor task.",
    untreatedTrajectory: "Without spatial ability feeding the motor system, novices in visuospatially complex tasks (e.g. laparoscopy, where the 3D field is viewed on a 2D screen) struggle more to build skill. Studies find visual-spatial ability is among the strongest predictors of early surgical-simulator performance, so a capable pair of hands lacking spatial orientation is disadvantaged at the outset.",
