    growthMeasures: "Reported correlations between spatial ability and novice surgical-simulator performance are moderate (around r ~ 0.39 in lower-experience groups) and drop toward zero (r ~ 0.02) with expertise. Honest read: spatial ability is a real early advantage, not a permanent one, practice substitutes for innate spatial talent over time. Findings are from modest simulator samples and vary by task.",
