    connectionCase: "Kristof-Brown, Zimmerman & Johnson (2005), meta-analyzing 172 studies and 836 effect sizes, found person-organization fit correlated about rho = .44 with job satisfaction and rho = .51 with organizational commitment, and person-job fit about rho = .56 with satisfaction. The honest catch: fit predicts attitudes far more strongly than it predicts actual job performance, where corrected correlations were weak (person-organization fit near rho = .07).",
