    connectionCase: "The most rigorous evidence is Virga et al. (2023), a pre-registered meta-analysis of 21 controlled workplace trials: strengths-use interventions produced small significant gains in workplace wellbeing (d ~ .31 post, .27 follow-up), general wellbeing (d ~ .24), and performance (d ~ .28). Schutte & Malouff (2019) found signature-strength interventions raised life satisfaction (Hedges g ~ .42) and happiness (g ~ .32) and reduced depression (g ~ .21). Ghielen et al. (2018)'s review found consistently positive but small outcomes.",
